slice: 06-decision-integrity
staged-diff-sha256: 8ae09b112deaa906eb87fb56a7513e539bee0e734b7c3cab84cdffe6bf4d0029
scope: follow-up applying batched-review findings over slices 02-06
review-rounds: 1 (data-integrity lens; three further lenses still running)
verdicts: PASS WITH FINDINGS

The reviewer confirmed from_state is reliably populated and all four unique_constraint
names match their migrations -- the two failure modes most likely to have broken this
slice silently. It then found a regression slice 06 introduced and two false claims.

Fixed here: approve_action was the one public function of seven missing slice 04's
else clause, which slice 06 made reachable and which raised MatchError in Demo.Runner;
FakeRepo never executed the Multi so the guards had zero executing coverage while the
findings claimed they were unit-tested; the "explicit fallback" claim was false and is
retracted in place; a tautological test that re-implemented the function under test was
replaced; "investigating" is not a CaseLifecycle status; Cases.transition_multi was
left unguarded; and the e2e framing tests raced the suite's own compilation.

Asserts: gates passed -- test 7 held (159 -> 168 tests), credo 77 held, dialyzer 43
held. The state guards now execute in tests, including their zero-row failure paths.

Does NOT assert: that the guards work against a live PostgreSQL, that any concurrency
was demonstrated, or that the three other review lenses have reported. Remaining
findings are recorded in BACKLOG.md rather than fixed.
